  "[says] Wang Lung expresses his dislike of his sons' cities.",
  "Wang Lung: \"Well, and what good is it for a man to wear a coat with a long tail to it and to walk about with a small round hat on his head, which is only for great lords and rich merchants? And what is this I hear of a new wife of yours?\"",
  "[action] sits and smokes pipe",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and what is this new wife of yours?\"",
  "[silence] (to Wang Lung) the second son says nothing.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Tell me about your new wife---is she fair?\"",
  "the second son (to Wang Lung): \"We have not yet brought her home.\"",
  "[says] Wang Lung expresses his reluctance to see his daughter-in-law.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Now, I do not know that I want to see her, for one does not know how to behave with a city wife. I am an old man and I have been too long from cities to know the ways of them.\"",
